+# CONTRACT — Real-Time Collaborative Document Editor
+
+## A. Build / Lint / Structure
+- [ ] `npm run build` compiles with no errors -> `tsc` exits 0
+- [ ] `npm run lint` passes -> `eslint src/` exits 0
+- [ ] `createApp(dbPath?)` exported from `src/server.ts` -> returns `{ app, start, stop }`
+- [ ] `start(port?)` listens (port 0 = random) and returns the actual port number
+- [ ] `stop()` closes HTTP server, WS server, and DB without hanging
+
+## B. OT core (src/ot.ts) — unit tested
+- [ ] `apply(content, insert)` inserts text at position (clamped) -> string check
+- [ ] `apply(content, delete)` removes range (clamped) -> string check
+- [ ] `transform(a,b)` insert/insert: a before b unchanged; a at/after b shifts by b.text.length -> convergence check
+- [ ] `transform` insert vs delete: shifts left when after deleted range; clamps to delete start when inside
+- [ ] `transform` delete vs insert: shifts right when insert before; shrinks to preserve insertion when insert inside
+- [ ] `transform` delete vs delete: overlap removed, positions adjusted, never negative length
+- [ ] `validateOp` rejects: non-object, bad type, negative/non-int position, missing text/length, length<=0 -> returns error
+- [ ] Convergence property: two concurrent inserts at same base, applied in both orders via transform, produce identical content with BOTH texts preserved
+
+## C. REST API — integration tested (supertest)
+- [ ] POST /documents {title, content?} -> 201, body has id, title, content, version (0)
+- [ ] POST /documents without title -> 400
+- [ ] GET /documents -> 200 array including created doc
+- [ ] GET /documents/:id -> 200 with content & version
+- [ ] GET /documents/:id (unknown) -> 404
+- [ ] PUT /documents/:id {title?,content?} -> 200, content updated, version incremented, new version row
+- [ ] PUT unknown id -> 404
+- [ ] DELETE /documents/:id -> 204; subsequent GET -> 404
+- [ ] GET /documents/:id/versions -> 200 array of versions (history)
+- [ ] GET /documents/:id/versions/:v -> 200 specific version content; unknown -> 404
+
+## D. WebSocket collaboration — integration tested
+- [ ] Connect to `/documents/:id` (ws) -> receives `{type:'sync', content, version, title}`
+- [ ] Connect to unknown doc -> error message then close
+- [ ] Send `{type:'op', op, version}` -> server applies, broadcasts `{type:'op', op, version}` to all clients (incl. sender ack)
+- [ ] Edit via WS is persisted -> GET /documents/:id shows new content & version
+- [ ] Two clients: client A's op is received by client B in real time
+- [ ] Malformed op -> server responds `{type:'error', message}` and does NOT crash; connection stays open
+- [ ] Concurrent edits: two clients send inserts at same base version -> both texts preserved, server converges
+
+## E. Robustness / persistence
+- [ ] 10 concurrent clients each send an insert on same doc -> no crash, all 10 texts present, server content consistent
+- [ ] Data survives restart: create+edit, stop(), new createApp(samePath), GET shows persisted content & versions
